findings.body:
The diff removed the `samples.is_empty()` guard. With an empty slice, `total` is 0 and `samples.len() as u32` is 0, so line 4 computes `0 / 0`. Integer division by zero panics in both debug and release builds. The doc comment on line 1 still promises 0 for empty input.

Trigger: Calling average(&[]), for example when a window or batch has no samples.}

Impact: Any caller that passes an empty sample set now panics instead of receiving the documented 0. This is a crash on a path the function explicitly documents as supported.
